 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nMySQL dialect generates incorrect SQL due to unreachable code\n\n#### Description\n\nThe MySQL dialect is generating incorrect SQL output due to unreachable code in several methods. Functions are returning early before executing their main logic, causing various SQL generation failures.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# Cast operations fail\nsql = \"CAST(x AS TIMESTAMP)\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(sql, read=\"mysql\", write=\"mysql\")[0]\nprint(f\"Expected: TIMESTAMP(x)\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n\n# Show profile operations fail  \nsql = \"SHOW PROFILE FOR QUERY 1 LIMIT 10 OFFSET 5\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(sql, read=\"mysql\", write=\"mysql\")[0]\nprint(f\"Expected: SHOW PROFILE FOR QUERY 1 OFFSET 5 LIMIT 10\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n\n# Function transformations fail\nsql = \"SELECT MONTHNAME('2023-01-15')\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(sql, read=\"mysql\", write=\"mysql\")[0]\nprint(f\"Expected: SELECT DATE_FORMAT('2023-01-15', '%M')\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n```\n\nThe issue affects multiple areas of MySQL SQL generation including cast operations, show statements, and function transformations.\n</issue>\n",
